# gitleaks baseline — manually verified, pre-existing, non-secret false positives.
#
# Every entry below was reviewed line-by-line (file, line, rule ID, and the
# actual matched text) before being added here. None of them are related to
# the Google primary-login feature or to CI infrastructure changes; all
# predate both. Full per-entry justification is recorded in
# docs/deployment/CLAUDE_GOOGLE_LOGIN_PRE_PRODUCTION_CHECK.md (deliberately
# summarized without reproducing the matched text here, to avoid this file
# itself re-triggering the same heuristics it documents).
#
# This file only suppresses `gitleaks dir` (working-tree snapshot) findings
# by exact fingerprint (file:rule:line). It intentionally does NOT disable
# any rule globally, and it is never used for the incremental `gitleaks git`
# scan of new commits (see feature-build-verify.yml), which must always
# come back with zero findings on its own.
#
# Never add Client Secrets, tokens, real emails, or `.env` contents here —
# doing so would mean the secret already leaked into the working tree, which
# is a "stop and rotate" situation, not an allowlist situation.

